  "prompt": "ACCESS POLICY:\nClub posts are public content that any authenticated user may read. Any user may create a post, and the author of a new post is the user who created it. A post may be edited or deleted only by its author or by an admin.\n\nENDPOINT: PUT /clubs/posts/{post_id}\nTARGET FUNCTION: app.routers.clubs.update_club_post (the handler of this endpoint)\n\nCODE:\n```python\n# file: app/routers/clubs.py\n@router.put('/clubs/posts/{post_id}', response_model=ClubPostOut)\ndef update_club_post(post_id: str, payload: ClubPostUpdate, current_user: User=Depends(get_current_user), db: Session=Depends(get_db)):\n    post = db.get(ClubPost, post_id)\n    if post is None:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail='Post not found')\n    if post.author_id != current_user.id and current_user.role != 'admin':\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail='Forbidden')\n    for field, value in payload.model_dump(exclude_unset=True).items():\n        setattr(post, field, value)\n    db.commit()\n    db.refresh(post)\n    return post\n```\n\nCONTEXT NOTE:\nOnly selected functions from the codebase are shown. Classes (including data models and schemas) and module-level variables are not shown.\nCalls not shown:\n- app.auth.get_current_user(...): defined in this codebase but not shown (call depth limit)\n- app.database.get_db(...): defined in this codebase but not shown (call depth limit)\n- db.get(...) called in app.routers.clubs.update_club_post: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- HTTPException(...) called in app.routers.clubs.update_club_post: not resolved by the extractor (imported), body not shown\n- payload.model_dump(exclude_unset=True).items(...) called in app.routers.clubs.update_club_post: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- payload.model_dump(...) called in app.routers.clubs.update_club_post: not resolved by the extractor (attribute_call), body not shown\n- db.commit(...) called in